bug_report:
C++ FE violates noipa attribute for nothrow
Consider:

[[gnu::noipa, noreturn]] void
foo ()
#ifdef DEF
{
  for (;;)
    ;
}
#else
;
#endif

struct S { ~S (); };

void
bar ()
{
  S s;
  foo ();
}

We get different behavior for -DDEF and without, in one case we assume foo can't throw and so bar doesn't have S::~S (); call, in the other we don't.
That is against the intent of the "noipa" attribute which is meant to make the function a black box where callers should work as if the function is not defined in the TU even when it is.
